            <ArticleTitle>Bronchodilators for patients with ischemic heart disease. How to avoid complications.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>324-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Treatment of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease and asthma with bronchodilating agents is more complex when the patient has ischemic heart disease. Drs Myers and Bogden recommend some precautions to help avoid potentially serious cardiac side effects in patients at risk.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
